<title>BELGIUM: Coceral sees EU 1997 winter grain area up 2.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Coceral sees EU 1997 winter grain area up 2.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The winter grain crop area in the 15 European Union member states is forecast rising by 2.5 percent to 24.1 million hectares for harvest in 1997, Coceral, the EU grain trade lobby said in a preliminary forecast on Friday.  </p>
<p>The EU 1997 soft winter wheat area was forecast rising 2.9 percent to 13.97 million hectares, winter barley by 1.3 percent to 4.78 million ha and durum wheat by 1.8 percent to 2.99 million ha.</p>
<p>The balance is made up of rye, which is seen 1.7 percent lower at 1.17 million ha, oats and triticale.</p>
<p>Coceral said that new data had not yet been received from Spain and Greece and last year's figures were used.</p>
<p>Heavy rain in Spain has delayed plantings while Greek figures will not be available until March.</p>
</text>
